WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.370
Hollywood history is littered with rags-to-riches
stories, though few of them are quite as literal

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.460
as Chris Pratt's.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.970
Now the face of Marvel's Guardians of the
Galaxy movies, Pratt has come an incredibly

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:15.870
long way since he dropped out of college at
17 after just a single semester, taking the

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.189
road less traveled on his way to Tinseltown.

00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:19.499
"I have a plan."

00:00:19.499 --> 00:00:21.390
"You've got a plan?!"

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.550
"Yes."

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.689
After cutting his teeth playing sidekicks
and funny men, the character actor was immediately

00:00:26.689 --> 00:00:32.059
promoted to the A-list when he won the role
of Marvel Studio's Peter Quill, aka Star-Lord.

00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:36.310
Turn back the clock a few years, however,
and there were definitely no red carpets or

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.310
caviar.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.310
So how did it happen?

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:42.609
Let's find out how Chris Pratt went from homeless
beach bum to Hollywood hotshot.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:46.780
After dropping out of school, Pratt had to
find ways to make ends meet, and he turned

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.190
out to be a natural at door-to-door sales.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.430
He worked as a coupon salesman for two years,
learning skills that he claimed served him

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.380
well when he finally made his dream move into
acting.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:59.399
His next gig was less white-collar — or
actually, more no-collar.

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:04.220
In need of a bit of extra cash, Pratt decided
to turn himself into what he described as

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.360
"a very, very low-rent Magic Mike."

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:12.020
"I would, just like slowly, awkwardly dance
and then take -- go down to my shorts and

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.310
they'd be like, 'Ohhh…'"

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:17.799
With next to nothing to lose and his twenties
looming, Pratt accepted an invitation from

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:22.260
an old friend who claimed to be living the
dream in Hawaii, and wanted his buddy to join

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:23.260
him.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:26.710
The two young men lived out of a van, which
Pratt admits had its ups and downs.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:28.460
On one hand, he was very free.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:33.509
But on the other, he had no bathroom and the
van had a bit of problem with fleas and rats…

00:01:33.509 --> 00:01:35.970
And of course, there was also the danger of
him turning into this:

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:44.859
"I am 35 years old, I am divorced, and I live
in a van down by the river!"

00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:49.390
One of the part-time positions Pratt picked
up in the Islands of Aloha was waiting tables

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:51.530
at a Bubba Gump seafood restaurant.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:55.670
It was while on shift at the diner that Pratt
had a chance encounter with Commando actress

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.960
— and shrimp fan — Rae Dawn Chong, who
was looking for actors for her comedy horror

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.070
short Cursed Part 3.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:06.759
After being impressed by his enthusiasm, Chong
flew Pratt to L.A. to give him a shot — and

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.940
ended up providing him with the platform he'd
been waiting for.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:14.050
Pratt’s next acting gig came when he landed
the role of Keenan in The Extreme Team, a

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:18.550
2003 Gen-X spy flick about a secret group
of Black Ops snowboarders.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:22.920
That movie sounds ridiculous, but in the grand
scheme it was just another rung in the ladder

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.950
that Pratt had to climb on his way to becoming
Star-Lord.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.640
Despite finally seeing himself as a professional
actor, things didn't exactly fall into place

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.720
right away in terms of auditions.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.900
Pratt made some cash doing commercials, but
eventually his persistence paid off, landing

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.440
him the part of high school jerk Bright Abbott
on the WB drama Everwood.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:46.010
Apparently, Pratt didn’t even really prepare
for this audition and landed the part by just

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:49.650
naturally being the type of character that
the directors were looking for — funny how

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.650
things work out.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:54.380
Pratt wasted no time getting comfortable on
the set of Everwood where he would end up

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:59.650
portraying Bright in 89 episodes between 2002
and 2006.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:04.580
When Everwood wrapped in '06, Pratt secured
a recurring role on long-running Fox favorite

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:09.800
The O.C., appearing in nine episodes as left-wing
activist — and occasional naked guitarist

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.160
— Che Cook.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.421
After these roles, Pratt finally landed what
most people consider his "big-break" with

00:03:15.421 --> 00:03:18.130
the role of Andy Dwyer on Parks and Recreation.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.220
"My full name is Andrew, I think.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.840
So… no?

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.540
Wait!

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.180
Yes."

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:28.190
"Let’s move on."

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:32.210
The critically acclaimed mockumentary opened
new avenues for Pratt, who attributes the

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:35.250
show's continued success to lead actress Amy
Poehler.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:39.860
Amazingly, Pratt’s character, Andy Dwyer,
was only supposed to appear in five or six

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:40.860
episodes.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:45.010
But when he turned out to be a fan-favorite,
he became part of the main cast for the show’s

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.010
entire run.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:50.180
"Leslie, I typed your symptoms into the thing
up here and it says that you could have 'network

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.080
connectivity problems.'"

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.160
The success of Parks and Recreation and the
cult following that started to build around

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.300
Pratt's character made movie studios pay attention.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:04.440
In the next few years, he had roles in 2011
Best Picture nominee Moneyball, Judd Apatow's

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:10.400
2012 comedy The Five Year Engagement, the
war drama Zero Dark Thirty and 2013’s Best

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.440
Picture nominated film, Her.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:16.760
With all of these strong big-screen performances
stacking up, it seemed like Pratt was poised

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.900
to shake the "funny friend" stereotype and
trade it up for something much bigger...

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:25.889
That much bigger thing would of course be
2014’s massive hit Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:04:25.889 --> 00:04:29.889
Director James Gunn admitted that when Pratt's
name first appeared on his desk, he scoffed

00:04:29.889 --> 00:04:32.590
at the idea of him leading the line as Star-Lord.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:37.099
Gunn even said that there was no way that,
quote, "The chubby guy from Parks and Rec"

00:04:37.099 --> 00:04:38.840
was going to star in his movie.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.889
At this point, Pratt had already been turned
down for the parts of James Kirk in the Star

00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:48.389
Trek reboot and Jake Sully in Avatar because
he didn't have the "it factor," and he himself

00:04:48.389 --> 00:04:51.110
was worried that he was "too fat to play a
superhero."

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:53.610
But in the end both he and Gunn were wrong.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:57.550
As soon as the director saw Pratt reading
for the part, he was sold — and apparently

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:01.580
knew he had found his Star-Lord just 20 seconds
into the audition.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:05.800
Just like that, the part was his, though that's
pretty much all Pratt knew for a good while.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:10.050
The actor has explained that his contact with
Marvel Studios was brief at that stage, to

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.930
the point where he wasn't even allowed to
see the screenplay.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:16.860
The radio silence lasted so long that Pratt
still had no clue what was happening when

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:19.090
he met up with Gunn to discuss the movie.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:23.110
Thankfully, that meeting went very well, and
was enough to calm Pratt's nerves.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:25.669
After that the actor was ready to become:

00:05:25.669 --> 00:05:26.780
"Star-Lord."

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.240
"Who?"

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.199
"I'm Star-Lord, man.

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:32.199
Legendary outlaw?"

00:05:32.199 --> 00:05:35.270
At that point, there was only one thing left
to do.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.900
Pratt tipped the scale at 300 pounds when
he went in to audition for Guardians of the

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.710
Galaxy, and it was only after winning the
role that he made a vow to shed some of it

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.740
— sixty pounds, to be exact.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:49.590
The actor lost the weight over a period of
six months using a workout that included running,

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.602
swimming, kickboxing and even a full triathlon.

00:05:51.602 --> 00:05:56.300
For some reason, however, dancing wasn't part
of his fitness regimen:

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.200
"Dance off, bro!

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.160
Me vs. you!"

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:00.300
"It's on!"

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:09.380
By the time the Guardians of the Galaxy shoot
began, Pratt looked like genuine superhero

00:06:09.389 --> 00:06:11.270
— with the six pack and all.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:15.740
This ripped bod, coupled with his undeniably
lovable personality, has helped Pratt’s

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.909
career take off, scoring him leading roles
in big movies like Jurassic World, Passengers

00:06:20.909 --> 00:06:22.830
and The Magnificent Seven.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:27.050
As Pratt's movie career continues to heat
up, one thing is becoming more and more clear.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:32.180
The guy is a seriously ripped, seriously funny
actor who isn’t going anywhere — except

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:34.449
right to the top of Hollywood’s A-list.

00:06:34.449 --> 00:06:39.040
Of course, no matter how famous he gets, Pratt
will always be this guy:

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.420
"Yup, yup.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.860
S--t my pants on camera.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:48.300
Check!"

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:49.389
Thanks for watching!

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:52.740
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.069
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

